Z||000000||C00LFLoYD||12-13-2001||12:26 AM||||Hey all, was wondering if anyone had any experience or thoughts about the front and rear coil over conversion offered by Shelby Custom? they want like 250ish for the rear, and 500ish for front.? was thinking about getting it, but wondered if anyone had any thoughts on them 1st. or something better for the money? thanx in advance!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bikemanj||12-13-2001||12:39 AM||||Do you have a link to their site? I am interested in coil overs too and would like to see what they have to offer.||||reg||5
Z||000002||C00LFLoYD||12-13-2001||12:49 AM||||Their web page is <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shelbycustom.com</A>  <BR>check it out, looks real sweet....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||Blacktree||12-13-2001||01:37 AM||||Hmmm... looks interesting. There are two nit-picks I can think of for now:<P>1) They don't specify the brand of coilover shock used in the front kit. Hopefully, an email or phone call can help you determine the brand and bound/rebound specs of those shocks.<P>2) The rear kits don't include struts. You'll have to buy a pair of struts and modify them. You'll also need to make sure the struts compliment the front shocks. Otherwise, you could end up with a stiff front suspension and loose rear suspension or vice versa.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bikemanj||12-13-2001||02:20 AM||||I agree with Blacktree. You could also consider looking here: <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com/standardfiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com/standardfiero.html</A> <BR>They are more expensive but they use Koni coilover shocks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||C00LFLoYD||12-13-2001||03:05 AM||||hmm, interesting point... thanx for pointing it out..... i didnt even realize the rears didnt come with the strut... (stinkin pictures) looks like they are out of the question then...... hmmm, what to get.... what to get then?<P>------------------<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||12-13-2001||04:03 AM||||you do realise that the coil over kit is designed to fit over your existing strut, correct?<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||12-13-2001||04:09 AM||||I tell you three times!<P>Held Motorsports! Held Motorsports! Held Motorsports! <P>Their coilovers are even on sale this month with the GP.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-13-2001||05:38 AM||||Coilovers are def the way to go. I may have missed something, but coil overs REPLACE the rear struts, not go with them. Maybe you meant shocks? Same with the front, they replace the front coil springs and shocks.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Daleford||12-13-2001||08:07 AM||||Coil-overs replace the rear strut UNLESS -- it is only a "coil-over conversion kit." Then the kit goes with your stock strut to produce a coil-over assembly.<BR>And at only $259, I believe that is what Cool Floyd is speaking off<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Blacktree||12-13-2001||10:09 AM||||The kit in the Shelby Customs website mentioned above is a conversion kit, similar to the one Held Motorsports sells.||||reg||1
Z||000011||RedHaze86SD4||12-13-2001||10:20 AM||||See now you guys got me curious about this I found on SummitRacing.com:<P>Material  Chrome Silicon Steel <BR>Finish  Powdercoat <BR>---------------------------------------------<BR>Lower your car and improve your handling.<BR>Pontiac: 1984-87 Fiero, 1.5 in. drop coil spring set<BR>Your car can have good looks and handling with these Suspension Techniques drop coil spring sets. These springs lower your car 1.5 in. to the level that the factory should have. Made of high quality chrome silicon steel, you will also notice an higher level of handling not found in mushy stock springs. Powdercoated for an attractive, durable finish.<BR>Sold in set of 4. $189.99<P>Any ideas here? Think it would be worth the purchase? Thanx<P>[edit]They also have KYB gas adjustable shocks for Fieros at $27.95 each.[/edit]<p>[This message has been edited by RedHaze86SD4 (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
